cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KŪPUNA-AI Bench, please cite it as below."
title: "KŪPUNA-AI Bench \"Let's talk story.\": Measuring Overrefusal and Harmful Compliance in AI Conversations with Older Adults"
type: software
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-08
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22667584
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22667583
    description: Concept DOI, resolves to the latest version
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JeremyGracey-AI/kupuna-bench-public"
abstract: >-
  An open-source evaluation of paternalistic withholding in AI conversations with older adults:
  multi-turn scenarios across end-of-life planning, hospice and palliative care, medications,
  driving cessation, grief and bereavement, and loneliness and companionship, scored per turn in
  two directions (overrefusal and harmful compliance) with severity S0-S3, paired age-cue variants,
  and a judge from a model family never under test, calibrated to expert labels.
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - benchmark
  - overrefusal
  - ai-safety
  - gerontology
  - older-adults
  - grounded-theory
